src/main.inset:39:24-39:50
`?` cannot leave a branch of a `fork`
this would leave one branch while the others run
help: give each branch a value, such as a `Result`, and handle the values after the `fork`, where every branch has finished

src/main.inset:40:13-40:18
a branch of a `fork` cannot change `total`, which every branch sees
this changes it
help: the branches run concurrently, so none may change what the others can see: give each branch a value, and gather the values after the `fork`

src/main.inset:41:18-41:22
a branch of a `fork` cannot change `seen`, which every branch sees
`push` changes `seen`
help: the branches run concurrently, so none may change what the others can see: give each branch a value, and gather the values after the `fork`

src/main.inset:44:24-44:30
a branch of a `fork` cannot change a table, and `insert` does
every branch sees this table
help: the branches run concurrently, so none may change what the others can see: give each branch a value, and write them to the table after the `fork`
